  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> identical shelves in which any number of shelves can be empty.</p><p>So, we will put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn></math> shelves empty one by one.</p><p>Also, the non-empty shelves won't require internal arrangement as all the shelves are identical.  </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> Shelf empty: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mn>1</mn></math> way</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> shelf empty: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mn>4</mn></math> ways</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> shelf empty: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mn>5</mn></math>ways</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> shelf empty: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mtable columnalign=\"left right\"><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mn>5</mn></math> ways</p><p>Total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math> ways</p>",
    "image": null
